---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'

const effectiveDate = 'March 18, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service & Master Services Agreement"
  description="ShorelineOps Care OS Master Services Agreement, Open Core Licensing Terms, and Clinical Dietary Safety Disclaimers."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <div class="relative py-16 sm:py-24 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Breadcrumb & Header -->
      <div class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/60 border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800/80 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-4">
          <Icon name="file-text" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
          <span>LEGAL AGREEMENT & MSA</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">
          Terms of Service & Master Agreement
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Effective Date: {effectiveDate} · Version 6.3.0 · Governing Open Core Software & Cloud SaaS Services
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Key Guarantees Frosted Card -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-xl border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-sm mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-bold font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4">Core Principles & Facility Guarantees</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="shield-check" class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Deterministic Safety</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Non-overridable IDDSI dysphagia and allergen hard-blocks protecting resident wellness.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="database" class="w-4 h-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Zero Vendor Lock-In</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">Your facility data belongs to you. Export complete records in JSON, CSV, or SQLite anytime.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <Icon name="lock" class="w-4 h-4 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Zero Data Resale</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">We never monetize, broker, or train third-party public AI models on resident health data.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Agreement Body -->
      <div class="space-y-10 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">01.</span>
            Structure of Agreement & Open Core Architecture
          </h2>
          <p>
            This Master Services Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into by and between <strong>Shoreline Operations LLC</strong> ("Shoreline", "we", "us") and the healthcare organization or healthcare dining operating entity ("Facility", "Subscriber", "you").
          </p>
          <p>
            Shoreline operates under an <strong>Open Core</strong> software model:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Community Open Core</strong>: The single-facility dietary operating engine (including local recipe scaling, offline kitchen sheets, HACCP temp logging, and local census roster) is licensed under the Free/Open Source Software terms published in our repository.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Commercial Cloud SaaS & Enterprise Modules</strong>: Proprietary multi-facility capabilities—including real-time PointClickCare EHR two-way sync, automated Dennis/Sysco split MRP purchasing, 3-way invoice matching, CMS-2567 federal survey binder compilation, and managed cloud backups—are governed exclusively by these commercial terms and active subscription tiers.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">02.</span>
            Clinical Care Responsibilities & Medical Disclaimer
          </h2>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-200">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">
              <Icon name="alert-triangle" class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400" />
              <span>Deterministic Enforcement Notice</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
              Shoreline Care OS provides algorithmic cross-referencing and deterministic guardrails for therapeutic diet orders, IDDSI 2.0 textures, and allergen exclusions. However, Shoreline is an operational tool and is not a licensed medical practitioner.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p>
            Facility medical directors, attending physicians, Certified Dietary Managers (CDM/CFPP), and Registered Dietitians (RD/RDN) retain sole clinical authority and responsibility for prescribing and verifying resident nutritional care plans. Shoreline deterministically enforces the clinical orders entered into the system (preventing delivery of non-compliant meals), but Facility remains responsible for verifying that EHR orders accurately reflect clinical assessments.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">03.</span>
            Subscriptions, Billing & Facility Licensing
          </h2>
          <p>
            Commercial SaaS subscriptions are billed monthly or annually per licensed facility bed/census tier. Payment is processed via credit card, ACH transfer, or distributor invoice credit arrangement.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>License Entitlement</strong>: Cloud features verify entitlement via cryptographic license keys signed with Ed25519 signatures. Offline grace periods allow continuous kitchen execution for up to 72 hours without active internet connection.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>No Surprise Seat Fees</strong>: Kitchen tablet kiosks, line cook stations, and nursing triage seats do not incur per-user license penalties. Subscriptions are priced transparently per facility.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cancellation</strong>: Subscriptions may be canceled with 30 days written notice before the next billing cycle.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">04.</span>
            Facility Data Ownership & Portability
          </h2>
          <p>
            Facility retains 100% legal ownership of all resident records, nutritional formulations, distributor contract pricing, and operational logs entered into Shoreline.
          </p>
          <p>
            In accordance with our <strong>Zero Vendor Lock-In</strong> guarantee, Facility administrators can generate a full database export (JSON, CSV, or SQLite snapshot) directly from the administration portal at any time, including upon termination of service. Shoreline will not withhold or delay data exports for any reason.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">05.</span>
            Service Level Agreement (SLA) & Offline Resilience
          </h2>
          <p>
            For Enterprise Cloud SaaS customers, Shoreline commits to a <strong>99.9% Monthly Uptime SLA</strong> for cloud API endpoints, excluding scheduled maintenance windows announced at least 48 hours in advance.
          </p>
          <p>
            Because healthcare dining cannot stop during internet outages, Shoreline implements local SQLite caching and IndexedDB offline mutation queues in every kitchen tablet kiosk. Line cooks can continue printing tickets, logging HACCP temperatures, and checking off meals offline; all pending records synchronize deterministically when connectivity is restored.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">06.</span>
            Limitation of Liability
          </h2>
          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, neither party shall be liable for indirect, incidental, punitive, or consequential damages arising from this Agreement. Shoreline's aggregate liability for direct claims under any commercial order shall be capped at the total fees paid by Facility in the twelve (12) months preceding the event giving rise to liability.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 7 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">07.</span>
            Governing Law & Jurisdiction
          </h2>
          <p>
            This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the <strong>State of Maine</strong>, without giving effect to conflict of laws principles. The parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts located in Cumberland County, Maine.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 8 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">08.</span>
            Contact & Legal Notices
          </h2>
          <p>
            Formal legal notices, audit requests, or inquiries regarding these Terms should be addressed to:
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono space-y-1 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            <div>Shoreline Operations LLC — Legal Affairs</div>
            <div>412 Commercial Street, Suite 400</div>
            <div>Portland, ME 04101</div>
            <div>Email: legal@shorelineops.com</div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Action Navigation -->
      <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-between items-center text-xs">
        <a href="/privacy" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-semibold">
          <span>Read Healthcare Privacy & HIPAA BAA</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
        <a href="/security" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white">
          <span>View Security Architecture & SLA</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
